    "result_text": "Done. Both new tests pass (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full build is green.\n\n## What I changed and why\n\nThe feature needed a persisted `registrationDate` that is (a) accepted optionally on `POST /api/owners`, (b) defaulted to the server's current date when omitted, and (c) returned as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` on `GET`.\n\n**Behaviour (kept as small, cohesive edits):**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added `registrationDate` (`format: date`, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is `allOf: [OwnerFields, \u2026]`, this one addition gives both the request DTO and the response DTO a `LocalDate registrationDate` (Jackson serialises `LocalDate` as `YYYY-MM-DD`, matching the tests' `today()`).\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 one `@Mapping` on `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` defaulting the date to `LocalDate.now()` when the DTO value is null. This method is used **only** on the create path (`BuildOwner`); the update path (`ApplyOwner`) sets fields by hand and doesn't touch it, so an update never clobbers an existing date.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 the `registrationDate` field plus a getter/setter (JPA uses field access here, MapStruct uses the accessors).\n\n**Persistence:**\n- Added a `registration_date DATE` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) so the entity is consistent across profiles.\n- Padded the positional seed `INSERT`s in `hsqldb/data.sql` and `mysql/data.sql` with `NULL` (the h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists, so they needed no change).\n\nI deliberately avoided adding logic to the already-complex `BuildOwner` step or introducing a new pipeline step + YAML wiring; the mapper default keeps the new behaviour as a single one-line mapping and touches no high-complexity method.\n\nThe test profile is `hsqldb`; I ran the full suite (`./mvnw -o test`) \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS, 2/2 tests passing**.",
